WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.150
I love riding over bridges!

2
00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:05.890
The water looks so pretty from here!

3
00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:12.250
Penelope, this is amazing!

4
00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:20.430
A minute ago, we were riding along the river, and now we’re riding in the river!

5
00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:20.430
Awesome.

6
00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:23.710
Hey, we’re passing by the Pentagon on our right!

7
00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:28.810
Penelope, you love riding over the water on a bridge.

8
00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:32.330
But I love riding under a bridge in a boat!

9
00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:34.670
Anna, look!

10
00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:37.550
An airplane is flying right over our heads!

11
00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:38.150
Wow!

12
00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:42.610
This is the closest I’ve ever been to an airplane in flight.

13
00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:47.610
Well, I’ve been inside a flying airplane.

14
00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:51.690
But not outside of an airplane as it flies over my head!

15
00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:55.410
And now we’re driving out of the water.

16
00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:58.070
I still can’t believe this thing drives and sails!

17
00:00:59.040 --> 00:00:59.710
I know.

18
00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:00.990
It’s amazing.

19
00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:08.350
After we ride along these railroad tracks, you’ll see my favorite part of the tour!

20
00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:13.530
The U.S. Treasury where they make money!

21
00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:17.190
That young man is making a lot of money, too.

22
00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:19.050
Did you hear these prepositions?

23
00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:19.810
On your left, on our right, in the river, over bridges, over our heads, over my head, on a bridge.

24
00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:24.250
As you watch more, look for 'inside' and 'outside.'

25
00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:27.650
Look, the U.S. Capitol is coming up!

26
00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:32.150
I have a great Fun Fact about the U.S. Capitol.

27
00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:33.850
What is it?

28
00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:36.470
There are tunnels under the Capitol.

29
00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:40.790
They connect the Capitol and office buildings of lawmakers.

30
00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:45.810
I bet they built them years ago for secret reasons!

31
00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:47.270
No.

32
00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:52.390
The lawmakers did not want to walk around outside in bad weather.

33
00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:53.090
Oh.

34
00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:58.070
We’re back at Union Station!

35
00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:03.650
Do you want to know a creepy Fun Fact about Union Station?

36
00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:06.970
The creepier the better!

37
00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:13.430
Many years ago, inside Union Station, there was a funeral home!

38
00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:15.810
A funeral home?!

39
00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:18.910
You mean, for dead people?!

40
00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:22.270
Do you know another kind of funeral home?

41
00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:23.870
No!

42
00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:28.730
Well, I’ve gotta run!

43
00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:30.750
Thanks for giving us the great tour!

44
00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:35.790
Captain, that was awesome!

45
00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:38.490
And your son is a great tour guide!

46
00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:39.070
What son?

47
00:02:39.500 --> 00:02:40.090
Him.

48
00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:43.130
I’ve never seen that boy in my life!

49
00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:44.810
See ya, ladies!
